Keep a shared powers as an empty list of whole numbers.
Place 1 into powers.
Place 2 into powers.
Place 4 into powers.
Place 8 into powers.
Place 16 into powers.
Place 32 into powers.
Place 64 into powers.
Place 128 into powers.
Keep a shared exponent as 0.
The target is 3.
Keep a shared ways as an empty list of whole numbers.
For every spot from 0 to target.
Place 0 into ways.

To seek from value (a whole number).
Set exponent to 0.
For every place from 0 to 7.
If item place of powers is at most value, set exponent to place.

To improve from step (a whole number) with power (a whole number).
The base is item power of powers.
The won is item (base minus 1) of ways.
The start is base minus 1.
For every shorter from 0 to power minus 1.
The offset is step minus start.
The addon is item shorter of powers.
The landing is offset plus addon minus 1.
The back is item landing of ways.
The candidate is won plus 1 plus shorter plus 1 plus back.
If candidate is less than item step of ways, set item step of ways to candidate.

Set item 0 of ways to 0.
For every step from 1 to target.
Seek from step.
The power is exponent.
The base is item power of powers.
The high is item (power plus 1) of powers.
The top is high minus 1.
The won is item (base minus 1) of ways.
If step is top, set item step of ways to power plus 1.
If step is not top, set item step of ways to won plus 1 plus 1 plus item (top minus step) of ways.
If power is more than 0, improve from step with power.

Show item target of ways.
